    "created_at": "2020-12-10T09:24:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-10T09:24:37Z",
    "body": "I had this same issue on IntelliJ IDEA's integrated terminal. @yacoob's [comment](https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/1842#issuecomment-719158776) helped me in fixing it. \r\n\r\nI did not face this issue on iTerm and VSCode (because they are smart enough to provide options to handle this). On IntelliJ IDEA, I could not find any setting in app for this.\r\n\r\nIterm:\r\n<img width=\"1014\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13679906/101751962-ef888700-3af6-11eb-8662-a344059a705f.png\">\r\n\r\nVSCode:\r\n<img width=\"769\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13679906/101751986-f7482b80-3af6-11eb-9836-15acdc55a8a8.png\">\r\n\r\n\r\nFrom what I have gathered, IntelliJ sets the locale using system language preferences. In my case, the system language was set to English India (en-IN) and IntelliJ had a hard time mapping it to en_IN.UTF-8. IntelliJ mapped it to C instead.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"185\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13679906/101750571-32e1f600-3af5-11eb-9c6c-d11204b5f867.png\">\r\n\r\nWhen I set my system language to English UK (en-GB), IntelliJ loaded the following locale and this fixed the issue for me :D\r\n\r\n<img width=\"204\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13679906/101751678-8e60b380-3af6-11eb-9c22-6f694c74415f.png\">\r\n",
